@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@
+# OBSERVABILITY
+
+Operator reference for the three observability surfaces of the single-host
+certified stack: Prometheus metrics (`/metrics`), distributed traces (OTLP to
+the internal collector) and the service objectives that sit on top of them
+([SLO.md](SLO.md)). Pair this with [ASSURANCE.md](ASSURANCE.md) (scheduled
+detection) and [INCIDENT.md](INCIDENT.md) (triage).
+
+## Traces (OTLP collector, retained)
+
+The realtime service emits OpenTelemetry spans when `OTEL_ENABLED=1`
+(production compose sets it). Instrumentation lives in
+`apps/realtime/src/instrumentation.ts`:
+
+- export is OTLP/HTTP to `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` (default
+  `http://otel:4318`);
+- sampling is parent-based at `OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG` (production `0.1`, i.e.
+  one in ten traces);
+- exported attributes are bounded (`url.path` and friends); do not add
+  person-identifying or secret attributes.
+
+The collector (`infra/otel/collector-config.yaml`,
+`otel/opentelemetry-collector` pinned by digest) now has two trace exporters:
+
+| Exporter | Destination | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `debug` | container stdout | live evidence (`docker compose ... logs otel`) |
+| `file/traces` | `/var/lib/otel/traces.json` on the `otel-traces` volume | retained, queryable OTLP-JSON |
+
+`file/traces` is a real retained sink, not just a log line. Delete the
+"retained only in debug" assumption from incident practice: an investigation
+can read spans produced while the collector was up.
+
+### Retention policy
+
+Rotation is bounded in `infra/otel/collector-config.yaml`:
+
+- `max_megabytes: 64` per file;
+- `max_backups: 5` (so at most ~6 files / ~384 MB total);
+- `max_days: 7` (older files are dropped);
+- `localtime: false` (rotate on UTC day boundaries).
+
+Traces are internal operational data, not customer records. Seven days is the
+default investigation window; raise it only with a disk-budget review (the host
+also runs the disk guard in the assurance lane).
+
+### Reading traces back
+
+The `otel` image is scratch-based and has no shell, so inspect the volume with a
+throwaway helper rather than `exec`:
+
+```bash
+# find the volume the compose project created
+vol=$(docker volume ls --format '{{.Name}}' | grep otel-traces | head -1)
+
+# print the retained batches (one OTLP-JSON object per batch)
+docker run --rm -v "$vol":/data busybox:1.38.0 \
+  sh -c 'cat /data/traces.json' | jq .
+```
+
+The file appends one OTLP-JSON object per export batch, so pipe through `jq -s`
+if a whole-document parse is needed. Prefer reading a copy so a live rotate
+cannot race the read.
+
+### Non-root write path
+
+The collector runs as uid `1001` with `read_only: true`, but a Docker-managed
+named volume is created `root:root`. The one-shot `otel-init` service in
+`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` chowns `otel-traces` to `1001:1001` before
+`otel` starts (`depends_on: service_completed_successfully`). If the collector
+starts and immediately logs a permission error on `/var/lib/otel`, confirm
+`otel-init` ran (`docker compose ... ps -a otel-init`).
+
+## Metrics lifecycle and restart semantics
+
+`/metrics` is rendered from in-process counters in
+`apps/realtime/src/server.ts` (`renderPrometheusMetrics`, `push`/`pushFamily`;
+`service="snowride-realtime"` is the only fixed label, and every other label is
+a bounded enum). These counters are **process-local**: `_bootTotal`,
+`_authFailures`, `_classificationFailures`, `runsValidated`/`runsRejected` and
+the rest reset to zero when the realtime container restarts.
+
+Durable history comes from the metrics snapshot timer. `startMetricsTimer`
+returns early when `METRICS_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL_MS <= 0`, so snapshots (migration
+`0053`) only accumulate when the interval is a positive value; production
+compose sets `METRICS_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL_MS: "300000"` (every five minutes). The
+`/launch-readiness` `sloBurn` flag is derived from the in-process
+`classificationFailures` and is therefore also reset on restart.
+
+What this means when reading dashboards and writing alerts:
+
+- **Treat a restart as a new series.** Do not compare a raw counter before and
+  after a restart, and prefer `increase()`/`rate()` with reset handling
+  (`resets()`) over subtracting raw samples.
+- **Detect resets explicitly** with `snowride_realtime_boot_total` and
+  `snowride_realtime_process_uptime_seconds` (or `process_start_time_seconds`
+  where scraped) so a deploy/recycle is not misread as a drop in traffic.
+- **Use snapshots for trends that must survive a restart.** Five-minute
+  snapshots are the durable record; a reset between snapshots leaves a short
+  gap that is expected, not an incident.
+- **Gauges are instantaneous**: `snowride_realtime_validation_in_flight`,
+  `_validation_queued`, `_rating_applications_in_flight`,
+  `_xp_applications_in_flight`, `active_sockets` and room counts describe the
+  current process only.
+
+## Quick checks
+
+| Question | Command / artifact |
+| --- | --- |
+| Are spans being retained? | `docker volume ls \| grep otel-traces`; read back with the helper above |
+| Is the collector up? | `docker compose -f infra/compose/docker-compose.yml ps otel otel-init` |
+| What did the collector last log? | `docker compose ... logs --tail=200 otel` |
+| Current objectives / burn | [SLO.md](SLO.md), `/launch-readiness`, the capacity lane in [ASSURANCE.md](ASSURANCE.md) |
